research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355713:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-40-$$\sum_{n} \frac{a_n}{S_n} \;=\; \sum_{n} \frac{1}{(n+1)\,H_{n+1}} \quad \text{diverges}, \qquad \sum_{n} \frac{a_n}{S_n^{2}} \;=\; \sum_{n} \frac{1}{(n+1)\,H_{n+1}^{2}} \quad \text{converges} .$$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355714:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-41-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355715:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-42-Classically these are written $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/(k H_k)$ and
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355716:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-43-$\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/(k H_k^{2})$, with $H_k = 1 + 1/2 + \dots + 1/k$.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355717:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-44-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355718:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md:45:**What the pair shows.** The harmonic series already diverges as slowly as any
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355719:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-46-explicit series on this page, and dividing its terms by the running total
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355720:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-47-produces something that diverges more slowly still. Dividing by the square of the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355721:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-48-running total overshoots into convergence. So the two exponents $1$ and $2$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355722:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md:49:straddle the boundary, and there is no last divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355723:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-50-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355724:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-51-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355725:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-52-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355726:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-53-**Given:** The sequence $a_k := 1/\iota(k+1)$, $k \in \mathbb{N}$, and its inclusive partial sums $S_n = \sum_{k=0}^{n} a_k$ ([[def-series]], [[def-finite-sum]], [[lem-of-naturals-positive]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355727:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-54-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355728:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-55-[L1] The canonical naturals are positive, so each $a_k$ is positive and each $S_n$ is a sum of positive terms ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355729:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-56-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355730:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-57-[L2] The harmonic series $\sum_{k \ge 1} 1/k$ diverges ([[ex-harmonic-series-diverges]]), and it is by definition the series of $j \mapsto 1/\iota(j+1)$ ([[def-series]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355731:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-58-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:355732:items/ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series.md-59-[L3] Abel-Dini: for a sequence of positive terms whose series diverges, with $S_n$ the inclusive partial sums, $\sum_n a_n/S_n$ diverges and $\sum_n a_n/S_n^{2}$ converges ([[thm-abel-dini]], [[def-integer-power]]).
