research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log:7533:research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:596721:+{"id":"fs-nth-term-test-converse","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter places the divergent harmonic series immediately after the nth-term condition precisely to show that terms tending to zero are not sufficient. The item turns that standard failed converse into an explicit false statement and refutes it with the same family under the local index convention. The numbered refutation is locally written.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
