research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log-8417-research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-679813-+{"id":"ex-sum-of-reciprocal-squares-converges","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Example 4.20 proves convergence of sum 1/n^2 by the same comparison 1/(n+1)^2<1/(n(n+1)) and obtains the upper bound 2. The item shifts that calculation to k>=2 and states the safe non-strict bound at most 2. Its verification follows the sourced telescoping comparison.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log-8418-research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-679814-+{"id":"ex-geometric-series-computed","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter gives the geometric sum formula and its starting-index convention. The two values 1 for sum_{k>=1}2^{-k} and 3/4 for sum_{k>=0}(-1/3)^k are direct specializations packaged together by the item. Their local arithmetic verification is not a traced source proof.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log-8419-research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-679815-+{"id":"ex-telescoping-sum-computed","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"Hunter Example 4.5 gives exactly sum_{k>=1}1/(k(k+1))=1 through the identity 1/(k(k+1))=1/k-1/(k+1). The item's verification is the same telescoping calculation with local dependency citations.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log-8420-research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-679816-+{"id":"ex-condensation-applied","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math331.pdf","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources apply condensation to the p-series and obtain the geometric ratio 2^{1-p}, with the threshold p>1. The item restricts to rational exponents, displays the algebra separately, and tabulates p=1/2,1,2. Its verification follows the sourced calculation under local rational-power notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
