research/audit/wave7-dispatch/certifier-a6-repair-fs-nth-term-test-converse-final.log-6892-research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/fs-nth-term-test-converse--47780c235cfbe92f.result.json-16-  "tail": "```text\nVERDICT: DEFECTS\n```\nFINDING 1\n  location: Remarks (second bullet)\n  severity: nonfatal\n  claim: \"Comparison, condensation, the root and ratio tests, Kummer, Raabe and Gauss all measure how fast the terms shrink, and each of them separates $1/k$ from $1/k^{2}$\"\n  evidence: The root test and the ratio test both yield limit 1 for the series $\\sum 1/k$ and $\\sum 1/k^2$, so they are inconclusive and do not separate these two series. The statement that *each* of the listed tests separates $1/k$ from $1/k^2$ is therefore false.\nBOUNDARY: Boundary cases were checked in the proof contract (zero limit, endpoint shift, nonempty choice from the Archimedean property). No boundary defects were found.\nSOURCES: All cited source items used in the refutation (cor-archimedean-reciprocal, lem-of-inverse-positive, def-real-limit, thm-p-series-rational, def-rational-power, thm-nth-roots-exist, def-integer-power, def-series, lem-of-naturals-positive) were inspected and each supports its usage in the target.\nCHECKED: The title, the public false statement, every numbered refutation step (1.1‑4.1), and the Remarks were read.\n```"
