research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699395-+> divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699396-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699397-+The two displayed series do not license the last clause. In the usual fixed
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:699398:+family $\sum 1/(kH_k^t)$, the Abel–Dini–Pringsheim threshold is divergence for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699399-+$t\le 1$ and convergence for $t>1$, so $t=1$ is precisely the divergent
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699400-+endpoint in the exponent order. The true no-slowest-series conclusion comes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-699401-+from applying the construction again to the newly obtained divergent series.
