research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725810-+## A2 defects and A3 repair proposals
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725811-+
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725826-+$1/(k\log k)$ is not absolutely summable, and a term of that order changes the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725827-+Bertrand borderline. In the model
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725828-+$a_k/a_{k+1}=1+1/k+c/(k\log k)+o(1/(k\log k))$, the value of $c$ distinguishes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:725829:+convergent from divergent logarithmically corrected harmonic series. It is not
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725830-+a harmless Gauss remainder. Thomson–Bruckner–Bruckner Theorem 3.41 and the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725831-+standard convergence-test statement instead use an error
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725832-+$O(k^{-\beta})$ for some $\beta>1$.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725845-+exponent restriction does not cost generality within the classical
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725846-+$O(k^{-\beta})$, $\beta>1$, hypothesis.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725847-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:725848:+### 2. `ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series`: false last-divergent claim
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725849-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725850-+Class: **(a) unambiguous falsehood**.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725851-+
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725855-+> divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725856-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725857-+The two displayed series do not license the last clause. In the usual fixed
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:725858:+family $\sum 1/(kH_k^t)$, the Abel–Dini–Pringsheim threshold is divergence for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725859-+$t\le 1$ and convergence for $t>1$, so $t=1$ is precisely the divergent
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725860-+endpoint in the exponent order. The true no-slowest-series conclusion comes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725861-+from applying the construction again to the newly obtained divergent series.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725864-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725865-+> So exponent $1$ gives a divergent member and exponent $2$ a convergent one.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725866-+> The absence of a slowest divergent positive series comes from applying
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:725867:+> Abel–Dini again to the newly produced divergent series, not from a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725868-+> last-exponent claim about this fixed pair.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725869-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725870-+### 3. `thm-limit-comparison-test` Fact L5 cites the wrong proposition
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725903-+- `thm-ratio-test` Fact L2 cites both `lem-limsup-exists` and
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725904-+  `def-limsup-liminf`, but no numbered step cites L2. Add `L2` to step 1.3,
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725905-+  where the limit superior is used as the infimum of the tail suprema.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:725906:+- `ex-harmonic-series-diverges` Fact L8 identifies the example as the $p=1$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725907-+  case of the p-series theorem, while the item expressly says neither proof
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725908-+  uses that theorem. Delete the unused L8 paragraph. The same identification
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-725909-+  remains, correctly cited, in the Example prose.
--
