research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734677-+> divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734678-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734679-+The two displayed series do not license the last clause. In the usual fixed
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:734680:+family $\sum 1/(kH_k^t)$, the Abel–Dini–Pringsheim threshold is divergence for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734681-+$t\le 1$ and convergence for $t>1$, so $t=1$ is precisely the divergent
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734682-+endpoint in the exponent order. The true no-slowest-series conclusion comes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734683-+from applying the construction again to the newly obtained divergent series.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734686-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734687-+> So exponent $1$ gives a divergent member and exponent $2$ a convergent one.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734688-+> The absence of a slowest divergent positive series comes from applying
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:734689:+> Abel–Dini again to the newly produced divergent series, not from a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734690-+> last-exponent claim about this fixed pair.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734691-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-734692-+### 3. `thm-limit-comparison-test` Fact L5 cites the wrong proposition
