research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769845-+{"id":"ex-condensation-applied","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math331.pdf","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources apply condensation to the p-series and obtain the geometric ratio 2^{1-p}, with the threshold p>1. The item restricts to rational exponents, displays the algebra separately, and tabulates p=1/2,1,2. Its verification follows the sourced calculation under local rational-power notation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:769846:+{"id":"ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abel%E2%80%93Dini%E2%80%93Pringsheim_theorem","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The Abel–Dini source explicitly applies the theorem to the harmonic series and records the logarithmically corrected family, while Hunter supplies the harmonic divergence. The item uses exact inclusive harmonic sums and selects exponents 1 and 2. The direct dependency application is locally written; its inaccurate 'no last divergent series in the family' sentence is an A2 defect.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769847-+{"id":"ex-raabe-decides-where-ratio-fails","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://people.math.sc.edu/girardi/m5545/TBB-AllChapters-Landscape.pdf","https://people.math.binghamton.edu/dikran/478/Ch5.pdf","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state that Raabe decides positive series whose ordinary ratio tends to 1 and give the p-series as the governing family. The item specializes to p=2 and computes R_k=2+1/(k+1) exactly, while the ratio tends to 1. This particular worked verification is locally composed.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769848-+{"id":"cex-ratio-inconclusive-root-decides","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.csudh.edu/~pong/a3/Notes_01.html"],"rationale":"The CSUDH notes use the same sequence 2^{(-1)^n-n}, compute alternating ratios 1/8 and 2, and obtain root limit 1/2 to show strict root-test dominance. The item translates that standard witness into the library's alternating-sequence interface and cites the earlier computation; its proof is an adapted sourced verification.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769849-+{"id":"cex-root-limit-one-decides-nothing","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convergence_tests"],"rationale":"The sources state that the root test is inconclusive at 1 and use p-series on opposite sides of the threshold. The item chooses p=1/2 and p=2, proves both root quantities equal 1 using the local nth-root lemma, and is therefore a worked semantic specialization. The detailed root calculation is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:769850:+{"id":"cex-comparison-needs-nonnegativity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The item is the standard direct-comparison theorem with its nonnegativity hypothesis removed, refuted by the negative harmonic series below the zero series. That is a recoverable alteration of the sourced theorem, not a novel mathematical claim. The explicit signed witness and verification are locally chosen.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769851-+{"id":"cex-condensation-needs-monotonicity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.rice.edu/~semmes/math331.pdf"],"rationale":"The item is Cauchy condensation with the sourced monotonicity hypothesis deleted. Its power-of-two zero set is a concrete local witness: the condensed series vanishes while the original terms equal 1 arbitrarily late. The false proposition is a recoverable alteration; the witness proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769852-+{"id":"cex-limit-comparison-l-zero-one-directional","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://sites.und.edu/timothy.prescott/apex/web/apex.Ch9.S4.html","https://www.math.ucdavis.edu/~hunter/intro_analysis_pdf/intro_analysis.pdf"],"rationale":"The UND statement gives only the direction from convergence of the larger comparison series to convergence of the smaller series when the quotient limit is zero. The item reverses that sourced implication and refutes it with the standard p=2 versus p=1 pair. The indexed verification is locally written.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
