research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769980-+$1/(k\log k)$ is not absolutely summable, and a term of that order changes the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769981-+Bertrand borderline. In the model
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769982-+$a_k/a_{k+1}=1+1/k+c/(k\log k)+o(1/(k\log k))$, the value of $c$ distinguishes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:769983:+convergent from divergent logarithmically corrected harmonic series. It is not
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769984-+a harmless Gauss remainder. Thomson–Bruckner–Bruckner Theorem 3.41 and the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769985-+standard convergence-test statement instead use an error
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769986-+$O(k^{-\beta})$ for some $\beta>1$.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-769999-+exponent restriction does not cost generality within the classical
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770000-+$O(k^{-\beta})$, $\beta>1$, hypothesis.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770001-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:770002:+### 2. `ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series`: false last-divergent claim
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770003-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770004-+Class: **(a) unambiguous falsehood**.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770005-+
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770009-+> divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770010-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770011-+The two displayed series do not license the last clause. In the usual fixed
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:770012:+family $\sum 1/(kH_k^t)$, the Abel–Dini–Pringsheim threshold is divergence for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770013-+$t\le 1$ and convergence for $t>1$, so $t=1$ is precisely the divergent
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770014-+endpoint in the exponent order. The true no-slowest-series conclusion comes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770015-+from applying the construction again to the newly obtained divergent series.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-770018-+
