research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778809-+## A2 defects and A3 repair proposals
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778810-+
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778825-+$1/(k\log k)$ is not absolutely summable, and a term of that order changes the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778826-+Bertrand borderline. In the model
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778827-+$a_k/a_{k+1}=1+1/k+c/(k\log k)+o(1/(k\log k))$, the value of $c$ distinguishes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:778828:+convergent from divergent logarithmically corrected harmonic series. It is not
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778829-+a harmless Gauss remainder. Thomson–Bruckner–Bruckner Theorem 3.41 and the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778830-+standard convergence-test statement instead use an error
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778831-+$O(k^{-\beta})$ for some $\beta>1$.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778844-+exponent restriction does not cost generality within the classical
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778845-+$O(k^{-\beta})$, $\beta>1$, hypothesis.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778846-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:778847:+### 2. `ex-abel-dini-pair-for-the-harmonic-series`: false last-divergent claim
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778848-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778849-+Class: **(a) unambiguous falsehood**.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778850-+
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778854-+> divergent series in the family.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778855-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778856-+The two displayed series do not license the last clause. In the usual fixed
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:778857:+family $\sum 1/(kH_k^t)$, the Abel–Dini–Pringsheim threshold is divergence for
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778858-+$t\le 1$ and convergence for $t>1$, so $t=1$ is precisely the divergent
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778859-+endpoint in the exponent order. The true no-slowest-series conclusion comes
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778860-+from applying the construction again to the newly obtained divergent series.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778863-+
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778864-+> So exponent $1$ gives a divergent member and exponent $2$ a convergent one.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778865-+> The absence of a slowest divergent positive series comes from applying
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log:778866:+> Abel–Dini again to the newly produced divergent series, not from a
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778867-+> last-exponent claim about this fixed pair.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-real-analysis-series.log-778868-+
